   1                             ; scsi16.ss:  NCR 53c720 scripts source for the Intel SSD Scsi-16 board
   2                             ;
   3                             ; Written Apr-May 1994 Wally Kramer, Step Technology, Portland, Oregon
   4                             ;
   5                             ; Purpose:
   6                             ;      This code performs the specific functions of a "scsi initiator" on
   7                             ;      behalf of a host processor.  Host I/O requests are translated into
   8                             ;      command, message_out, data_in or data_out, message_in, status
   9                             ;      sequences to accomplish the requested I/O.  When I/O is complete,
  10                             ;      the host is signaled so it can perform the complete_io portion of
  11                             ;      the driver.
  12                             ;
  13                             ; Conventions:
  14                             ;      Generally, instructions changed by runtime modification "patching"
  15                             ;      (not to be confused with what NCR calls "patching" which is really
  16                             ;      load time relocation) have the PATCH symbol used in the instruction
  17                             ;      as a place holder.  Generally such an instruction has a label of
  18                             ;      the form xxx_n where xxx is describes the functional procedure as a
  19                             ;      unique but suggestive name and n is a digit, always increasing down
  20                             ;      the file.  This saves creative effort and helps identify where
  21                             ;      patches are done.
  22                             ;
  23                             ;      ??? indicates things which may need further research or testing
  24                             ;      to determine validity or appropriateness.  So far, these have all
  25                             ;      been NCR questions.
  26                             
  27                             ;      !! indicates code which was changed to allow debugging.
  28                             ;
  29                             ; Modifications:
  30                             ;      27 June 1994, Wally Kramer
  31                             ; Since 21 June, added sigp bit clear instruction in schedular; added lots of
  32                             ; assert statements (presently commented), added LED control; moved assign of
  33                             ; req_tbl_ptr to before selection for selection timeout host error processing.
  34                             ;
  35                             ;      29 June 1994, Wally Kramer
  36                             ; Added write of req_tbl_ptr into req_done_q in io_complete.
  37                             ;
  38                             ;      30 June 1994, Wally Kramer
  39                             ; Removed debugger stuff
  40                             ;
  41                             ;      26 July 1994, Jerrie Coffman and Vineet Kumar
  42                             ; Clean up more debugger stuff that Wally left in by mistake.
  43                             ; Added more asserts.
  44                             ;
  45                             ;      11 August 1994, Jerrie Coffman
  46                             ; Using absolutes for bss label accesses does not produce releative
  47                             ; addressing in the output code.  Replaced absolute names with bss?+n
  48                             ; lables to allow code to be relocatable.  Updated and cleaned up
  49                             ; some comments.
  50                             ;
  51                             ;      23 August 1994, Jerrie Coffman and Vineet Kumar
  52                             ; A selection does not halt the script processor.  The script processor
  53                             ; will continue running until another instruction is executed which
  54                             ; requires the SCSI bus or a select timeout occurs.  Added a "jump when"
  55                             ; instruction following the selection to force a pause until the selection
  56                             ; phase is complete.
  57                             ;
  58                             ;      18 November 1994, Jerrie Coffman
  59                             ; Corrected a coding error in save data pointers following a phase mismatch.
  60                             ; The calulation for the new scatter/gather entry length and address fields
  61                             ; was incorrect.  They were being adjusted by the amount remaining to be
  62                             ; transferred instead of the amount that was just transferred. 
  63                             ;
  64                             ;      7 December 1994, Jerrie Coffman
  65                             ; Added a global labels "msg_sent" and "cmd_sent" placed immediately after
  66                             ; the SCSI message out and command transfer instructions.  These can be used
  67                             ; by the interrupt handler to detect a phase mismatch during message out or
  68                             ; command phase and recover by simply restarting the script from the current
  69                             ; location.
  70                             ;
  71                             ;      11 March 1995, Jerrie Coffman
  72                             ; Added jump to bad_error if actual phase does not match expected phase
  73                             ; following a selection.
