 687                             
 688                             ; If a phase mismatch occurs, the 720 is halted and interrupts the host--all
 689                             ; beyond our control (and against our desires).  This happens when a target
 690                             ; disconnects mid transfer (changes to msg_in phase to send a disconnnect
 691                             ; message, maybe because it wants to seek a different track, or, for a raid
 692                             ; controller, talk to a different drive).
 693                             ;
 694                             ; To gracefully recover, the host checks for a phase mismatch interrupt,
 695                             ; executes the phase_mismatch C code (below) and sets us (the 720) running.
 696                             ; If we had our druthers, the "chmov" instruction would accept an alternate
